{"answer": "The Danish message (`TOOL_BUDGET_MESSAGE_DA`) must be a single, non-empty Danish string that promises nothing concrete. Per issue #151's requirements, it may not contain:
- a `<` character;
- any digit;
- a phone number, email address or opening hour;
- the words `ring`, `minutter` or `timer`;
- a named channel, time or person;
- a persona name;
- any claim to be a person (the EU AI Act Art. 50(1) check, applied in the negative).

The message is also kept free of booking and customer data. Issue #498 notes that the shipped wording ends with "En kollega vil følge op på din henvendelse." and that this follow-up promise is now questioned while no escalation destination exists.", "sources": ["issue-151", "pull-439", "issue-498", "specs/support-agent-escalation/spec.md"]}

